<title>UK: LME lists another U.S. delivery point for copper.</title>
<headline>LME lists another U.S. delivery point for copper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The London Metal Exchange (LME) has approved the port of New Haven in the U.S. as a good delivery point for copper.</p>
<p>It will take effect from May 14, 1997, the LME notice said.</p>
<p>Until now New Haven has been listed as a good delivery point for tin, lead, zinc, primary aluminium and nickel.</p>
<p>London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7771</p>
